\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Summing values that transform together}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{An observable on a pair of configurations may have
opposite values at the two points. If the configurations
carry equal scalar weights, its sum can be calculated
without choosing an inverse for the number of points.
For values in a representation with several components,
which part can remain after the same invariant summation?}
